    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nnot works for some operator func\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nprepare `test.lua`:\n```lua\nlocal function test_operator(motion)\n\tif motion == nil then\n\t\tvim.o.operatorfunc = test_operator\n\t\treturn \"g@\"\n\tend\n\tlocal pos = vim.pos.cursor()\n\tlocal line = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(pos.buf, pos.row, pos.row + 1, false)[1]\n\tvim.print(line)\n\tpos.col = #line\n\tvim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, pos:to_cursor())\nend\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gm\", test_operator, { expr = true })\n```\n\n1. `nvim --clean --noplugin -u test.lua`\n2. some text:\n```text\naaaa\nbbbbb\ncccccc\n```\n3. place cursor on each word beginning, and enable follow motion:\n<img width=\"557\" height=\"372\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2240738-0b6c-4c30-b91b-a582643b9416\" />\n\n4. type `gmil`, the result:\n<img width=\"466\" height=\"367\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3eec87b2-8304-4f1e-b5a3-e0fad10335b7\" />\n\n`:messages` all output:\n<img width=\"667\" height=\"114\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ba62288-50da-4152-a6a0-4cf0e9b91e3c\" />\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n4. after type `gmil`, the result should be:\n<img width=\"472\" height=\"290\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cb045bf4-f119-4a4a-87c6-b938db739c6d\" />\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1473+g9a29622b54\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n6.18.26.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwindows terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\ngithub download page",
