            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "That's how it's designed. If you use multicursor, there is still only one cursor, in addition to that there are multiple marks (what you see as multicursor).\nSo if your function uses `nvim_win_set_cursor()` there is only \"one\" (the real one) cursor replaced.\nWhat you want is to update those multicursor marks too.\n1. Update Cursor\n2. Update Multicursor marks\n\nFor your function this could be helpful: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/41601\n",
            "created_at": "2026-09-02T08:09:27Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41612#issuecomment-5506521447",
