            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It's true that `nvim_win_set_cursor` is a \"programmatic\" operation, but it happens within a mapping, so it should still be replayed per-cursor. The mapping itself is real user-input, and that's all that matters (in theory) when deciding whether an action is replayable.\n\nThis may be a CmdAtom misclassification bug. Will look into it.",
